From: mattephi <ialentev@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:41:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] UWLab port patches on top of release/3.0.0-beta2

Two changes needed to run UWLab's OmniReset cube-stack task on this branch.

1. simulation_cfg.py: make SimulationCfg.physics eager and backend-selectable.
   Upstream defaults it to None and lets SimulationContext substitute PhysxCfg()
   at init (simulation_context.py:166-169), but env cfgs tune physics in
   __post_init__, which runs first and therefore hits None. The default is now
   chosen from UWLAB_PHYSICS_BACKEND (physx | newton, default physx), which lets
   one Isaac Lab checkout serve both the PhysX and the Newton branch of UWLab.

2. wrench_composer.py: hasattr(self._asset.data, "body_com_pos_w") is a TYPE
   check -- the code says so, it avoids isinstance to dodge a circular import --
   but calling it on the INSTANCE evaluates the property, which queries the PhysX
   backend. During the first initialize callback the backend has no transforms
   yet and raises a plain Exception, which hasattr does not swallow (it only
   swallows AttributeError). Checking the class performs the intended test
   without touching the backend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhuUnim6biTdbSspBfCgm5
